 - **Main Interface (Common)**: Moved **minimap to the right-edge** for quicker read. Add **details** to most **progress bars**; e.g. in the Tech bar `Fusion: 2245 / 5774 (35)`. Show **chars in the GP bar even if 100%** (e.g. `Great Scientist: Lyons (3) - [RESEARCH_CHAR] 100%`) Change in [GPUtil.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/GPUtil.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5514+) **Swap top left** (e.g., Treasury) **and top right** (e.g., Turn and Year) **text position**, and optionally **move commerce sliders to the right side** (allows to freely expand advisors so they use the entire left side, and is visually closer to scoreboard and most mouse controls) **in city screen or map view**. Show **Era text default ON** (as of now on top left); **strip " Era" suffix** so text is now only e.g., `Renaissance` not `Renaissance Era` (would overflow during golden age when text is upscaled, plus it is unneeded). See [Main interface rework](/README.md#main-interface-rework).
-- **Main Interface (City Screen)**: Enhanced with a new **Great Person +n ICON** information in relevant Buildings' rows; added a new **Specialists Breakdown** and **Culture Breakdown**; added **optional extra rows** in the **Production Chooser Bar** and **optionally hide the unit bar** (`"PlotListPanel"`) (note: does not affect the production chooser outside of the city screen); added **Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the **Production Queue**; fixed some hard anchored items that now **dynamically** adjust to sides' width. **Beautified** it as well: removed the 3 gray bars ("Trade Routes", "Buildings", "Specialists"), increased sides' width, made bonuses columns even in width, and other changes. These changes allow to now display more information and reduce the need for scrolling or hovering. Also **enlarged** the **Bottom-Left** and **Bottom-Right** panels so they align dynamically with the enlarged **Side Panels**. Enhanced the **city bar** and **other bars**, e.g., `Lakamha: 16 - 12372 (4500BC)` or `Growing - 30/43 (4 Turns)`. Split the **Draft group** into hurry controls on the right (and a **new draft button**) and config options on the right. Add building list filtering buttons ("Show All Buildings", "Show Regular Buildings Only", "Show National Wonders Only", "Show World Wonders Only"). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5526+) Reduce **food/production top bars' size** so text does not overflow when upscaled (also helps preserve overall distance to side panels due to increasing base font size from body to label). Change in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). And other changes. See also [KI#101](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#101---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-gp-bar-tooltip-in-city-screen-not-showing-gp-from-obsolete-buildings-yet-seemignly-counting-them-for-the-total-gp-calculation).
+- **Main Interface (City Screen)**: Enhanced with a new **Great Person +n ICON** information in relevant Buildings' rows; added a new **Specialists Breakdown** and **Culture Breakdown**; added **optional extra rows** in the **Production Chooser Bar** and **optionally hide the unit bar** (`"PlotListPanel"`) (note: does not affect the production chooser outside of the city screen); added **Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the **Production Queue**; fixed some hard anchored items that now **dynamically** adjust to sides' width. **Beautified** it as well: removed the 3 gray bars ("Trade Routes", "Buildings", "Specialists"), increased sides' width, made bonuses columns even in width, and other changes. These changes allow to now display more information and reduce the need for scrolling or hovering. Also **enlarged** the **Bottom-Left** and **Bottom-Right** panels so they align dynamically with the enlarged **Side Panels**. Enhanced the **city bar** and **other bars**, e.g., `Lakamha: 16 - 12372 (4500BC)` or `Growing - 30/43 (4 Turns)`. Split the **Draft group** into hurry controls on the right (and a **new draft button**) and config options on the right. Add building list filtering buttons ("Show All Buildings", "Show Regular Buildings Only", "Show National Wonders Only", "Show World Wonders Only"). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5526+) Reduce **food/production top bars' size** so text does not overflow when upscaled (also helps preserve overall distance to side panels due to increasing base font size from body to label). Change in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5689+) Adjust **city camera** to the north (tunable) so extra rows can be shown without overflowing into bottom BFC plots in `CvGame::onCityScreenChange`. And other changes. See also [KI#101](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#101---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-gp-bar-tooltip-in-city-screen-not-showing-gp-from-obsolete-buildings-yet-seemignly-counting-them-for-the-total-gp-calculation).
 - **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5503+) Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5507+) **Main Interface (civilization flag):** **Removed the civilization flag** from the production buttons bar (next to minimap) to show more buttons instead and have a more efficient display. Instead, added **optional compact top-left civilization flag** (with same preserved BtS hover/click behavior) (if **enabled**, left **top text spacing is shifted to make room for the compact flag**). Unlike base AdvCiv, this **optional flag** is **also visible in city screen** because it does not interfere with bottom city-action buttons. This flag is useful to know player civ, hover for player traits, and click to capital's city screen. Default disabled (tunable) as it can be distracting and undesired.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5533+) **Scoreboard**: do **not draw beyond** bottom of commerce sliders (previously it would overflow beyond top of the screen), add **+ (up) and - (down) scroll buttons** to choose **first and last leader shown** when the **number of leaders is high** (e.g., if there are 48 leaders to display and the scoreboard can only show ~30 leaders max). Note: the Info screen's score tab allows to see all leaders so this is a fine trade-off to avoid vertical overflow. Add a **Lock scoreboard hover toggle button** so scoreboard is always hovered on even without hover (e.g., to see power ratios without having to hover). Note: in first turns of the game this effectively has no effect since power ratios are not yet visible. Change in [Scoreboard.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/Scoreboard.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See [README.md (Scoreboard)](/README.md#scoreboard)

